A||N||2||Fiero_Freak||3.4 Heads....Which ones?||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero_Freak||03-31-2001||06:05 PM||||  My 3.4 is from a 95 Camaro.  I've read some posts that say to use the 2.8 Fiero Heads...and some that say you should use the 3.4 heads?  Are there any difference?  I thought that they were esentially the same thing?  Any opinions?  Which I should rebuild?  Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steven||03-31-2001||06:55 PM||||Those heads are the same as the 2.8 Fiero, but as for the heads to rebuild? I would rebuild the heads that have the least miles. You could also take a look at the valves themself. The head with the cleanest valves are the ones that would have seen the least abuses. I had two sets of heads, and took the ones with the least miles. Told the machine shop to put in bronze valve guides. The next day he called me to make sure that I wanted the guides, because the orginal guides were in excellent shape, and were tighter now than they would be if he put the bronze guides. That saved me about a hundred bucks. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_Freak||04-01-2001||02:22 PM||||Cool...I was hoping they were the same.  The Camaro heads were barely even bronzed....not like my current heads...  which I also pulled about a 1/2 pound of crud out of.||||reg||14
